Z||000000||87FieroGTx||06-26-2001||01:35 AM|||| I just got done driving a 3.8s/c all I can say is WoW!! Its just to easy to smoke the tires with the 3800s/c but when you want you can git it to hook up nicely. <P> After I got done we raced me in my 94 Trans Am V8 manual around 300hp him in the 85 SC/SE? 3.8 auto 280hp he seemed to hook up and pull away real quick and stayed about 2 cars ahead the whole way to 80mph.<P><BR> One thing I noticed was that the rear end seemed to break lose if you hit the gas to hard in corners.<P> I was thinking of doing a 3.4 turbo swap but now I'm thinking of droping that and going with the 3800.<P> Does anyone know how much HP the 3800 trans can hold? If I git the 3800 I want one of thoes Intercoolers from ace) 350hp sounds nice. <P> Is the ACE 3.8 blower/Intercooler upgrade reliable?||||reg||10
Z||000001||stimpy||06-26-2001||11:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87FieroGTx:<BR><B> Is the ACE 3.8 blower/Intercooler upgrade reliable?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ain't supercharged Fieros a kick in the ass?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> As far as the whole intercooler upgrade goes, does it even exist? Why are there no pictures of it on the website? Can the Clutters even produce the name of a customer who has had one installed? My opinion? Smoke and mirrors. <P>For REAL products, see Chris West.<P>(disclaimer- I am not a representative or employee of WestCoast Fieros. I don't even hang out at the shop. I have seen his work and the aftermath of an ACE conversion. If I had the $ for a 3.8 myself, Chris would get the job)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||06-26-2001||11:44 AM||||Yes an intercooler does exist.<P>Get the 3800SC parts from here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.thrasher-ep.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thrasher-ep.com/</A> <P>The best aftermarket source for 3800's<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">      <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals. &lt;b&gt; New White Face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS&lt;/b&gt;Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||06-26-2001||01:05 PM||||The intercooler raises the blower 2.6" which meands you would have to modify your deck lid. Just the intercooler and smaller blower pulley gives about 300HP ('bout 240 at the wheels) Chris West has headers and Thresher racing has modified heads, all of that plus a little water/alcohol injection will probably get you into the 300HP at the wheels range. <P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||06-26-2001||03:09 PM||||I checked the engine bay on a late MR2, supercharged and intercooled. Its a pretty flat compact intercooler and I think a place can be found to put in a Fiero pretty ez. Ill be looking in yards when I go to them for one to put in my turbo.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
